  "id": "KG-2026-11-05-a",
  "title": "Ghar se call, number kata!",
  "format": "Musical: a Housie game where every call from home gets the same sung chorus 'Ring ring! Number kata!' from the whole kitty",
  "idea": "Shruti makes a rule that every call from home costs a Housie number; the calls get sillier (charger, namak, fridge), and then her own silent phone lights up with her husband asking how many cooker whistles.",
  "logline": "Shruti rules that every call from home costs a Housie number, her friends keep losing numbers to silly calls, and then her own husband calls asking how many cooker whistles.",
  "game": "every call from home gets the chorus 'Ring ring! Number kata!' and one number cut, ordinary (charger), ordinary (namak), absurd (where is the fridge), then the rule maker herself",
  "experiment": {
    "type": "musical",
    "hook": "Housie cage spinning, Shruti announces 'Naya rule! Ghar se call, number kata!' while Ruhi's phone is already lighting up in her hand, chip 'GHAR SE CALLS: 0'",
    "variable": "a sung chorus refrain 'Ring ring! Number kata!' from ALL on a beat after every call (4 times), so the reel plays like a song with a counting chip",
    "hypothesis": "a repeating chorus the viewer can predict and chant keeps people to the end: watched above 35% and skip under 50%, and a 'ghar se call during kitty' moment every woman lives should earn 3+ shares"
  },
