    "notes": "Fixed version of KG-2026-11-04-b (QA: voice pace 2.21 w/s, a 6.2 s shot). Same musical test, story and cast. Voice pace raised 28 to 34 (KG-2026-11-02-a passed the same check with a pace bump), mid-line question marks and commas cut so the voice does not pause (Haan beta, charger drawer mein hai!), and every two-line shot over 8 words split into two shots (ball 22 / namak, ball 90 / fridge, Naya rule / Ghar se call), so no shot has more than 8 words. Answer line now Teen seeti! so a muted viewer gets the cooker joke. 17 shots, about 40 s. Real kitty scene (calls from home in the middle of Housie, named in team feedback). Lead is Shruti (last reel's lead was Myra), with her strict hisaab flavour ('Barabar hisaab!'). One rule pinned as a counting chip so a muted viewer always knows the stake. Game played 3 times (charger, namak, fridge) then flipped on the rule maker, the same shape that made the door-arrivals winner work (host breaks her own rule, opening line thrown back), here tested as a musical. Twist is a see-it phone screen. Claim before reveal: Shruti brags 'silent pe hai' right before her screen lights up. The 'Teen!' chorus answer is the laugh: every woman knows the seeti count. Endings tried: Shruti switches every phone off (flat); husbands all on one group call (too many people, confusing); the rule thrown back with the chorus (kept, loops into the opening). Kind humour, no money troubles."
  },
